t to accomplish in career and life, and gain the experiences and skills to get there. We'll help you manage the academic, social, and personal stressors, and assist you in developing your own toolbox of coping strategies and approaches to overcome the challenges. Did you know that first-year undergraduate students have access to their own Personal Student Success Team ? This program is available to all first-year undergraduate students regardless of major or commuter/residential status. And it doesn’t stop after your first year. As you grow and develop here, we’ll be there! Academic Resources for Current Students Career Resources for Current Students Navigating Your Path to Academic & Career Success Your Personal Student Success Team Before even stepping foot on campus, you'll make immediate connections with a wide-range of support including a: Faculty mentor to guide your academic success Peer mentor in your major to help you get acclimated academically and socially Student affairs liaison to connect you with contacts and resources across campus Librarian to assist with academic research PRIDE Mentoring Program for New First-Year & Transfer Students The PRIDE Mentoring Program offers personalized support to new first-year and transfer students through one-on-one and group workshops, along with academic, social, cultural, and leadership development activities. Designed to help students thrive, the program supports: Improving academic performance Adjusting to college life Building connections across campus Gaining insight into academic culture Developing leadership skills Forming meaningful relationships with peers, faculty, and staff Learn more about PRIDE Mentoring Program Academic Support Services Our team of caring professionals provides academic coaching, tutoring, and support to keep you on track. We monitor your progress and use early assessment and retention alert programs to identify struggling students and offer timely assistance. Academic Advising, Coaching & Tutoring Click to Open In your academic program, you will be matched with a compassionate and committed professor who will act as your personal advisor and mentor. Your advisor will: Offer guidance on which classes to take, and the kinds of internships, extracurricular opportunities, and other hands-on experiences to pursue to best position you for career success. Help you find an internship or job thanks to their many industry and field connections. Help walk you through a change in major if you're looking for a new direction. Academic coaching is provided through one-on-one sessions or group meetings with a trained academic coach who will assist you in a variety of areas, including: Study skills to enhance learning and memory of academic information Organization and time management Test taking and test anxiety Academic planning and preparation for pre-registration of courses Textbook reading Note-taking Tutoring is available for most introductory and upper level courses to help you navigate concepts and classes. Our trained staff of students is available for one-on-one sessions. Access student resources for academic advising, coaching & tutoring on mySuccess Exploratory Studies Click to Open Not sure what you want to study? Our Exploratory Studies program will pair you with an advisor who will help you figure that out. And if you find that the path you chose is not the right one, we can help you find a new direction. Changing majors is not only possible, it's perfectly normal. Learn more about Exploratory Studies Access student resources for Exploratory Studies on mySuccess Student Accessibility Services Click to Open The Office of Student Accessibility Services provides services to students with learning disabilities, physical disabilities, and psychological disabilities. The office serves as a campus advocate to ensure that all have equal access to academic programs and other aspects of campus life. Learn more and access student resources for accessibility services on mySuccess Math & Writing Centers Click to Open At our Writing Center, highly-trained English and communications instructors will help you tackle all kinds of writing assignments. They will help guide you through everything from brainstorming and researching a topic, to organizing, outlining, drafting, and revising the paper. The Writing Center is open to both undergraduate and graduate students. Learn more about the Writing Center on mySuccess Our Math Center provides individual tutoring in mathematics for all students. Experienced professional and undergraduate tutors provide help with all courses with mathematics content. It all adds up to helping you succeed! No appointment is necessary. The Math Center is open to both undergraduate and graduate students. Learn more about the Math Center on mySuccess Career Support Services Whether an undergrad, grad, or non-traditional student, we'll help find the right career path. Develop the skills you need from day one to achieve your goals and reach professional success. Our student-centered approach guides you on your journey, whether you have a clear path or not. Personal Career Counseling with Career Design & Development Click to Open At Widener University, we prioritize your career development by providing personalized guidance through our Office of Career Design and Development. Through this office, you will have the opportunity to work closely with your assigned career counselors in a one-on-one setting. These dedicated professionals are committed to helping you identify your passions and align them with your professional and personal aspirations. This unique relationship with your career counselor is of utmost importance, as they will not only know you by name but also by your dreams. They will invest the time and effort to understand your individual goals, interests, and aspirations, ensuring that the guidance they provide is tailored specifically to you. By fostering this meaningful connection, we aim to empower you on your career journey and support you in translating your passions into tangible opportunities. Your career counselor will be your trusted ally, offering valuable insights, resources, and strategies to help you navigate the path to success. Learn More About Career Design & Development Meet the Career Design & Development Team Co-Op, Internship & Student Job Experiences Click to Open At Widener, we offer invaluable hands-on career experiences through internships, externships, clinicals, our acclaimed co-op program, and other opportunities, distinguishing you in your career. Located near Philadelphia, you have easy access to world-class companies and organizations, amplifying networking and collaboration prospects. These experiences and our strategic location accelerate your career and position you as a competitive professional in the dynamic job market. Learn more about co-ops & internships Access co-op, internship & student job resources for current students Handshake: Recruiting and Career Management Platform Click to Open Handshake stands as Widener's foremost recruiting and career management platform, catering to both students and alumni. This premier platform enables students to effortlessly connect with employers, submit applications for various job positions and internships, and conveniently register for career-related events. Employers, on the other hand, benefit from Handshake's capabilities to identify highly qualified candidates and efficiently manage their on-campus recruiting activities at Widener. With Handshake's comprehensive features, both students and employers can streamline their recruitment and career management processes, fostering successful connections and opportunities within the Widener community. Explore Handshake Learn more about Career Design & Development WidenerCONNECT: Networking and Mentorship Community Click to Open As a student joining WidenerCONNECT, you'll have exciting opportunities to: Broaden and personalize your Widener network according to your individual interests and professional goals. Connect with Widener alumni residing in various locations worldwide, spanning from your hometown to destinations abroad. Discover experienced alumni mentors who can provide valuable guidance and support you along the Inside Track, starting right away. Cultivate long-lasting relationships that extend beyond your time at Widener and consider paying it forward by becoming an alumni mentor yourself upon graduation. WidenerCONNECT opens doors to expand your network, forge meaningful connections, and nurture relationships that can shape your personal and professional journey. Embrace these invaluable opportunities and make a lasting impact within the Widener community. Join WidenerCONNECT Learn more about Career Design & Development Student Success & Support Stories Widener Unveils Campus Enhancements Ahead of Fall Semester New residence hall, relocated campus store, additional dining options and other expanded student amenities highlight summer 2026 improvements at Widener. A New Home, A New Hope for Future Health Professionals One year after the closure of Crozer-Chester Medical Center, the Diagnostic Medical Sonography and Radiologic Technology programs are thriving in their new home on Widener’s Chester campus. Carrying Our Legacy Forward: New Website Connects Generations Through PMC History Widener’s roots as Pennsylvania Military College still echo across the university today. The newly launched PMC website honors its role in the university’s history and helps carry its story forward for future generations. Get in Touch Academic Wellbeing on MySuccess Career Resources on mySuccess Handshake Job Board Student Success and Academic Enrichment 528 E. 14th Street 610-499-1266 studentsuccess@widener.edu Career Design & Development 526 E. 14th Street 610-499-4176 careers@widener.edu Widener Career Design & Development Facebook Widener Career Design & Development X Widener Career Design & Development Instagram One University Place Chester, PA 19013 1-888-WIDENER Facebook Widener Instagram LinkedIn Widener TikTok Twitter Youtube Interactive Campus Map Apply to Widener Directions, Parking & Transportation Explore All Programs Work at Widener © 2026 Widener University Widener University uses IP2Location.io IP geolocation web service. Campus Safety Report It Privacy Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.widener.edu/why-widener/career-inside-track": {
      "title": "Career Inside Track",
      "description": "Career Inside Track | Widener University Skip to main content Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Utility Menu WU Links myWidener mySuccess Canvas Outlook Email Office365 Zoom Self Service Wolfgram Library Campus Store Resources For You High School Students New First-Year & Transfer Students Current Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Community & Partners News Events Athletics ♥ Give Mega Nav Academics Academics Academics Overview Find Your Program Explore All Programs Undergraduate Majors Graduate & Law Programs Adult & Continuing Studies Online Programs Colleges & Schools College of Arts & Sciences College of Health & Human Services School of Business Administration School of Engineering Dwyer School of Nursing Center for Continuing Studies Commonwealth Law School Delaware Law School Resources for Success Academic & Career Support Accessibility Co-Ops & Internships Study Away Wolfgram Library Academic Calendar Catalogs & Handbooks Faculty Directory Labs & Learning Spaces Academic Leadership Close Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Overview Admissions Pathways Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Transfer International Military & Veteran Tuition & Aid Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Visit Campus Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Apply Now Check Application Status Request Info Close Why Widener Why Widener Why Widener Overview Career Inside Track Faculty Mentorship Research & Innovation Leadership Development Location Matters Student Stories Alumni Success Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Close Campus Life Campus Life Campus Life Overview Our Campus Campus Vibe Where to Live Where to Eat What's Nearby Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Athletics & Club Sports Music & Performing Arts Fraternity & Sorority Life Well-Being Belonging Mental Health & Counseling Health & Fitness Personal & Community Safety Engage Widener mySuccess WidenerCONNECT Student Engagement & Transformation Leadership Close About About About Overview About Widener Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Our Leadership Strategy, Mission & History Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Community Resources Clinics & Centers Wolfgram Memorial Library Observatory Taylor Arboretum Faculty Directory Offices & Departments Maps & Directions Work at Widener President's Leadership Team Close Search Website AI Search Apply Visit Search Website AI Search Mega Nav Academics Find Your Program Explore All Programs Undergraduate Majors Graduate & Law Programs Adult & Continuing Studies Online Programs Colleges & Schools College of Arts & Sciences College of Health & Human Services School of Business Administration School of Engineering Dwyer School of Nursing Center for Continuing Studies Commonwealth Law School Delaware Law School Resources for Success Academic & Career Support Accessibility Co-Ops & Internships Study Away Wolfgram Library Academic Calendar Catalogs & Handbooks Faculty Directory Labs & Learning Spaces Academic Leadership Admissions & Aid Admissions Pathways Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Transfer International Military & Veteran Tuition & Aid Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Visit Campus Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Apply Now Check Application Status Request Info Why Widener Career Inside Track Faculty Mentorship Research & Innovation Leadership Development Location Matters Student Stories Alumni Success Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Campus Life Our Campus Campus Vibe Where to Live Where to Eat What's Nearby Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Athletics & Club Sports Music & Performing Arts Fraternity & Sorority Life Well-Being Belonging Mental Health & Counseling Health & Fitness Personal & Community Safety Engage Widener mySuccess WidenerCONNECT Student Engagement & Transformation Leadership About About Widener Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Our Leadership Strategy, Mission & History Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Community Resources Clinics & Centers Wolfgram Memorial Library Observatory Taylor Arboretum Faculty Directory Offices & Departments Maps & Directions Work at Widener President's Leadership Team Apply Visit Utility Menu WU Links myWidener mySuccess Canvas Outlook Email Office365 Zoom Self Service Wolfgram Library Campus Store Resources For You High School Students New First-Year & Transfer Students Current Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Community & Partners News Events Athletics ♥ Give Career Inside Track Whether you’re pursuing an undergraduate degree or elevating your career in one of our powerhouse graduate programs, here, from day one, you'll be an insider. Why Widener Career Inside Track More in this section… Click to expose navigation links on mobile. Why Widener Career Inside Track Faculty Mentorship Research & Innovation Leadership Development Location Matters Pride Perspectives On the Inside Track, You'll Set Your Future in Motion First job, career change, big promotion—at Widener, no matter what your future holds, you'll prepare for outsized success. As our students often say, you'll take the inside track to wherever you're going. Start by learning from industry insiders who know your field and your personal aspirations, inside and out. Gain experience that matches your career goals. Build a marketable skillset and make critical professional connections. When you hit the job market (or interview for that promotion), you'll feel confident and assured. Your experience will prepare you for the moment—when you land the job, earn the promotion, or receive the grad school acceptance letter. It all starts on the inside track. Distinguished Faculty—Your Industry Insiders Our faculty are prominent figures in their fields. They steer research and shape practices that inform the future of your profession. They have a network of connections directly related to your future path. When you arrive at your next workplace, you'll feel the value of their knowledge, insights, and advice. Learn More About Our Faculty Career Counselors—Your Support System Through one-on-one meetings with career counselors, you'll prepare to achieve your short-term goals (that next job) while focusing on long-term career success (the leadership roles that follow). These counselors will dig in with you, listening as you describe your goals, dreams, and concerns. You'll graduate ready to start fast and advance quickly in your field. More About Individual Career Support Industry Ties—Your Insider Advantage At Widener, you won't have to look far to build your professional network. In fact, you may not need to look at all. You'll make connections initiated by your professors. You'll stay in constant contact with alumni. You'll form bonds with co-op, internship, and field supervisors. And you'll take advantage of Widener's reputation in your industry. With this network by your side, you'll be well positioned for success. State-of-the-Art Facilities—Your Future Workplace We're home to state-of-the-art academic facilities, including our nursing simulation, robotics engineering, and finance labs, plus a fully-equipped television studio. These spaces provide you with the type of hands-on experiences you need to succeed. Even as \"the new person\" on the job, you'll serve as an expert in the tech, trends, and tools of your field. Explore Our Campus Student Perspectives You can take what you learned in the classroom and then apply that to the real world. If we're going over a lecture and we're talking about framing and then we go out to a job and they're doing metal or wood framing, you can see how. Semaj Smith-Barber Class of 2028 Undergraduate | Construction Management Read Semaj's Story Student Perspectives As a former Marine, it helps that Widener is a Yellow Ribbon school--whatever the GI Bill doesn't cover Widener will forgive. I plan to get my bachelor’s, work in a hospital, then I can get into flight nursing and practice trauma care. Samuel Flood Class of 2027 Undergraduate | Bachelor of science in nursing Read Samuel's Story Student Perspectives Camp has always been such a big part of my life... I think the education I got through Widener really helped me to fuel that passion and helped me to make connections that I didn’t know could have been made. Sophia Hastings Class of 2018 Undergraduate | Social Work; Gender, Women & Sexuality Studies Read Sophia's Story Student Perspectives Working at Widener's Community Nursing Clinic is a really unique experience that a lot of schools don't have to offer. It’s real life scenarios where we are able to relate to it cause it's around us. Taylor Wise Class of 2025 Undergraduate | Bachelor of science in nursing Read Taylor's Story Student Perspectives Performing Gameday Satisfaction Market Research for the Philadelphia Union was unforgettable. We got an in-depth look at fan, stadium worker, and media reporter insights on the Philadelphia Union, Subaru Park, and loyal fanbase. The energy was palpable. Ahmad Kamara Class of 2024 Student Perspectives I loved having the opportunity to do research, but also having the opportunity to research with a large medical device company—that’s something you don’t see quite often. Shaylyn Westmoreland Class of 2023 and 2024 Graduate | Biomedical Engineering Read Shaylyn's Story Flexible Degree & Career Paths Our programs help you plan for a career (and a life) that's bound to take on many forms. Personalize Your Career Track Here, you can turn your passions and curiosities into a career worth leading. Work one-on-one with career counselors to map your plan A (and your plan B, in case you change your mind). Customize your education by adding a minor or a double major, or enrolling in one of our dual degree graduate programs. You'll end up with a tailor-made education that suits your personal and professional interests and opens doors for jobs, promotions, and graduate study. Finish Your Degree Faster Through one of our accelerated program options, you'll turn your long-term goals into short-term accomplishments. All of our undergraduate majors can roll into an accelerated graduate degree. That means you can earn both a bachelor's degree and a master's degree, graduate a year early, and save a year of tuition. Your advanced education will put you on the inside track to higher-level positions and earning potential. Prepare for the Jobs of the Future Twenty years ago, students didn't train for careers in app development or drone operation. The job market keeps evolving. But don't fret: here at Widener, you'll prepare for today and tomorrow. You'll learn from students and faculty across many programs, gaining a broader interdisciplinary view of your work. You'll learn to think critically, solve problems from new perspectives, and quickly adapt to new technology. And by adding a minor or certificate to your degree, you'll acquire diverse skills that help you thrive in any setting. Powerhouse Programs Recognized by experts and valued by students and alumni, our programs serve as a launchpad for life. Region's 1st Undergraduate Robotics Engineering Major Widener offers Pennsylvania’s first undergraduate robotics major, and one of very few nationwide. Renowned in the Region The Dwyer School of Nursing was ranked 7th in Pennsylvania among private colleges. Source: Nursing Schools Almanac Ranked 11 out of 50 On the list of Editors' Choice 50 Best Accredited PsyD Programs for 2022 Source: psydprograms.org A Top MBA in PA Recognized among the state's elite online MBA programs. Source: Online MBA Today Top Health Care Management Program in PA Ranked top 5 in health care management programs in Pennsylvania. Source: U.S. News & World Report 2025 Best Law Schools Delaware Law School and Widener Law Commonwealth nationally ranked by the Princeton Review. Source: Princeton Review Start by Exploring Our Degree Programs Not sure which program would best suit your interests and career goals? Reach out to an admission counselor; we're here to help! Explore All Programs Contact Our Admissions Department Keep Exploring Find Your Program Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Flexible Associate's & Bachelor's Degrees More on the Widener Advantage Faculty Mentorship Leadership Development Research & Innovation Location Matters One University Place Chester, PA 19013 1-888-WIDENER Facebook Widener Instagram LinkedIn Widener TikTok Twitter Youtube Interactive Campus Map Apply to Widener Directions, Parking & Transportation Explore All Programs Work at Widener © 2026 Widener University Widener University uses IP2Location.io IP geolocation web service. Campus Safety Report It Privacy Consumer Information"
