      "description": "Career Design & Development | Widener University Skip to main content Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Utility Menu WU Links myWidener mySuccess Canvas Outlook Email Office365 Zoom Self Service Wolfgram Library Campus Store Resources For You High School Students New First-Year & Transfer Students Current Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Community & Partners News Events Athletics ♥ Give Mega Nav Academics Academics Academics Overview Find Your Program Explore All Programs Undergraduate Majors Graduate & Law Programs Adult & Continuing Studies Online Programs Colleges & Schools College of Arts & Sciences College of Health & Human Services School of Business Administration School of Engineering Dwyer School of Nursing Center for Continuing Studies Commonwealth Law School Delaware Law School Resources for Success Academic & Career Support Accessibility Co-Ops & Internships Study Away Wolfgram Library Academic Calendar Catalogs & Handbooks Faculty Directory Labs & Learning Spaces Academic Leadership Close Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Overview Admissions Pathways Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Transfer International Military & Veteran Tuition & Aid Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Visit Campus Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Apply Now Check Application Status Request Info Close Why Widener Why Widener Why Widener Overview Career Inside Track Faculty Mentorship Research & Innovation Leadership Development Location Matters Student Stories Alumni Success Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Close Campus Life Campus Life Campus Life Overview Our Campus Campus Vibe Where to Live Where to Eat What's Nearby Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Athletics & Club Sports Music & Performing Arts Fraternity & Sorority Life Well-Being Belonging Mental Health & Counseling Health & Fitness Personal & Community Safety Engage Widener mySuccess WidenerCONNECT Student Engagement & Transformation Leadership Close About About About Overview About Widener Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Our Leadership Strategy, Mission & History Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Community Resources Clinics & Centers Wolfgram Memorial Library Observatory Taylor Arboretum Faculty Directory Offices & Departments Maps & Directions Work at Widener President's Leadership Team Close Search Website AI Search Apply Visit Search Website AI Search Mega Nav Academics Find Your Program Explore All Programs Undergraduate Majors Graduate & Law Programs Adult & Continuing Studies Online Programs Colleges & Schools College of Arts & Sciences College of Health & Human Services School of Business Administration School of Engineering Dwyer School of Nursing Center for Continuing Studies Commonwealth Law School Delaware Law School Resources for Success Academic & Career Support Accessibility Co-Ops & Internships Study Away Wolfgram Library Academic Calendar Catalogs & Handbooks Faculty Directory Labs & Learning Spaces Academic Leadership Admissions & Aid Admissions Pathways Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Transfer International Military & Veteran Tuition & Aid Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Visit Campus Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Apply Now Check Application Status Request Info Why Widener Career Inside Track Faculty Mentorship Research & Innovation Leadership Development Location Matters Student Stories Alumni Success Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Campus Life Our Campus Campus Vibe Where to Live Where to Eat What's Nearby Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Athletics & Club Sports Music & Performing Arts Fraternity & Sorority Life Well-Being Belonging Mental Health & Counseling Health & Fitness Personal & Community Safety Engage Widener mySuccess WidenerCONNECT Student Engagement & Transformation Leadership About About Widener Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Our Leadership Strategy, Mission & History Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Community Resources Clinics & Centers Wolfgram Memorial Library Observatory Taylor Arboretum Faculty Directory Offices & Departments Maps & Directions Work at Widener President's Leadership Team Apply Visit Utility Menu WU Links myWidener mySuccess Canvas Outlook Email Office365 Zoom Self Service Wolfgram Library Campus Store Resources For You High School Students New First-Year & Transfer Students Current Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Community & Partners News Events Athletics ♥ Give Career Design & Development At Widener, you won’t just start your career at graduation. You'll continue the work you’ve been doing all along. Academics Academic Resources for Success Academic & Career Support Career Design & Development More in this section… Click to expose navigation links on mobile. Academic & Career Support Career Design & Development Meet the Career Design & Development Team From Day One Whether you're an undergraduate, graduate, or non-traditional student, we’ll help you find the career path that's right for you. From the moment you arrive on campus, you will develop the skills and experiences you need to reach your goals. It’s not just about landing that first job or next job – though that’s important, too. It’s about placing you on the inside track to a lifetime of professional success. Finding Your Path Our student-centered approach starts with helping you figure out who you are and where you want to go in life. Not everyone has a clear path in mind, and that’s okay. And sometimes you start down one path and realize it’s not the right one. We will meet you where you are, and guide you on this journey. Through our Office of Career Design and Development, and your interactions with industry-connected professors, you will get the kind of personalized attention and support to help you navigate all the twists and turns, design the pathway of your choice, and hone the skills you need to achieve your dreams. Career Resources for Current Students on mySuccess Support at Your Fingertips Industry-Connected Professors Click to Open Our professors are not only amazing educators, they're leaders in their fields and have deep industry ties, offering you essential connections to the profession you’re about to enter or advance in. Proximity to Philadelphia Click to Open Our location in Greater Philadelphia means we've got links to world-class companies and organizations in and around the city, including Comcast, Boeing, Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, Merck, Vanguard, and others. Personal Career Counselors Click to Open You’ll work one-on-one with your assigned career counselors - through our Office of Career Design and Development – to identify and connect your passions to professional and personal aspirations. This is a key relationship for you, as they will get to know you not only by name but by dream. Meet the Career Design & Development Team Tools of the Trade Click to Open Our robust tools and technologies will help you develop and hone the skills you need to be competitive - from networking to resume and CV writing to interviewing. And we have resources to help you search for internships and jobs, including Handshake , our premier recruiting tool for students, alumni, and employers. Visit What Can I Do With This Major to explore the many career paths within different majors in addition to employers, professional associations, specialized jobs, and graduate programs. Plus we have resources especially useful for our graduate students across the academic programs, designed to be flexible as you may be balancing school with work and family responsibilities. For example, you can practice and polish your interview skills 24/7 through Big Interview , a platform for students and experienced professionals alike. Programs & Events Click to Open Industry and discipline-specific career fairs, networking events, clinics, graduate school preparation, and other programs mean that no matter what you choose to study, you’ll have the right resources at your fingertips. Our programs and events are open and designed for all students - undergraduate, graduate, and non-traditional alike. Our clinics, for instance, are scheduled in late afternoons and early evenings to accommodate both students and working professionals. Proven. Results. Career Success for Class of 2025 93% achieved their career goals—employment, graduate school, or military/service—within 6 months of graduation, per Widener University research. $70,300 Early Career Salary for Widener's undergraduate alumni Source: PayScale $116,100 Mid-Career Salary for Widener alumni with a bachelor’s degree, which ranks in the top 22% nationwide Source: PayScale Hands-On Career Experience You will gain invaluable hands-on experiences through internships, externships, clinicals, our acclaimed co-op program, and other opportunities that will help accelerate your career and distinguish you from others. And our proximity to Philadelphia means you have easy access to world-class companies and organizations. Co-Ops & Internships Alumni Pay it Forward Our alumni are generous with their time and talent to help the next generation succeed. Many come back to campus to speak with current students about their own experiences and welcome students to shadow them, or extend internship or co-op opportunities. Some of these connections even lead to full-time jobs, making that Widener link truly something special. Info for Employers Hire Widener Looking to hire interns, co-op students, or full-time employees? Look no further than Widener. Our students are career-ready thanks to beyond-the-classroom, hands-on experiences and our strong emphasis on honing professional skills. We work closely with employers to connect leaders like you to these future trailblazers. Hire Widener Info for Alumni Pride for Life Our alumni are part of the Pride for life. As a graduate, you have access to career guidance, including personal consultations, help updating your resume/CV, assistance making a strategic career transition, access to professional skills workshops and career fairs, and more. Resources for Alumni In the News And the Emmy Goes To… Communication studies alumni Dakarai Daniel and Andrew Proctor – back together collaborating on projects – scored an Emmy for their work with the Washington Commanders. Career Impact Communities Aim to Broaden Student Career Horizons Career Design and Development recently launched its free, not-for-credit Careers by Design Canvas course as a one-stop resource for students and faculty to access all that Career Design & Development has to offer. Students Experience MORE! Opportunities with Donor-Funded Internships The Experience MORE! program helps financially support students who need summer break to work and earn money. The program instead makes it possible for them to do unpaid or low-paid internships that will help prepare them for rewarding careers. Upcoming Events October 5 • 02:00 PM Civil & Construction Management Career Fair Build Connections. Shape Your Future. Step into opportunity at the Civil Engineering & Construction September 16 • 02:00 PM School of Business Administration Career Fair September 21 • 10:00 AM Rapid Resume Review Sessions September 30 • 12:00 PM Boeing Employer Session Student Perspectives You can take what you learned in the classroom and then apply that to the real world. If we're going over a lecture and we're talking about framing and then we go out to a job and they're doing metal or wood framing, you can see how. Semaj Smith-Barber Class of 2028 Undergraduate | Construction Management Read Semaj's Story Student Perspectives As a former Marine, it helps that Widener is a Yellow Ribbon school--whatever the GI Bill doesn't cover Widener will forgive. I plan to get my bachelor’s, work in a hospital, then I can get into flight nursing and practice trauma care. Samuel Flood Class of 2027 Undergraduate | Bachelor of science in nursing Read Samuel's Story Student Perspectives Camp has always been such a big part of my life... I think the education I got through Widener really helped me to fuel that passion and helped me to make connections that I didn’t know could have been made. Sophia Hastings Class of 2018 Undergraduate | Social Work; Gender, Women & Sexuality Studies Read Sophia's Story Student Perspectives Working at Widener's Community Nursing Clinic is a really unique experience that a lot of schools don't have to offer. It’s real life scenarios where we are able to relate to it cause it's around us. Taylor Wise Class of 2025 Undergraduate | Bachelor of science in nursing Read Taylor's Story Student Perspectives Performing Gameday Satisfaction Market Research for the Philadelphia Union was unforgettable. We got an in-depth look at fan, stadium worker, and media reporter insights on the Philadelphia Union, Subaru Park, and loyal fanbase. The energy was palpable. Ahmad Kamara Class of 2024 Student Perspectives I loved having the opportunity to do research, but also having the opportunity to research with a large medical device company—that’s something you don’t see quite often. Shaylyn Westmoreland Class of 2023 and 2024 Graduate | Biomedical Engineering Read Shaylyn's Story Keep Exploring Resources for Students Career Resources on mySuccess Co-Op, Internship & Student Job Resources on mySuccess Resources for Alumni Information for Alumni Resources for Employers Hire Widener Get in Touch Career Resources on mySuccess Handshake Job Board Meet the Team Career Design & Development 526 E. 14th Street 610-499-4176 careers@widener.edu Widener Career Design & Development Facebook Widener Career Design & Development X Widener Career Design & Development Instagram Janet R. Long Associate Vice President, Career Design & Development Office of Career Design and Development 526 E. 14th Street (610) 499-4045 jrlong@widener.edu Julie Abrams Director of Professional Development, Career Design & Development 526 E.14th St. 610-499-1271 jabrams@widener.edu One University Place Chester, PA 19013 1-888-WIDENER Facebook Widener Instagram LinkedIn Widener TikTok Twitter Youtube Interactive Campus Map Apply to Widener Directions, Parking & Transportation Explore All Programs Work at Widener © 2026 Widener University Widener University uses IP2Location.io IP geolocation web service. Campus Safety Report It Privacy Consumer Information"
